d #uuid "af69649b-ba41-5eae-bb14-bde36a03c4ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-35754" :question/problem "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $A$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $A$ has $2$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st and $2$nd columns." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-35754/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1a557d6-52f3-5df3-8088-5b875296e72e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-35754"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-35757/selection/eeb4d250eb178da53234cb863d7d7469d2bab9f37bb1bcec382bcd3c0eb032eb" :answer/id #uuid "11d23bb6-76e7-513c-9c6c-11c276a62fbe" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$st, $2$nd, and $4$th only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35757/selection/02b0be138d8a0f39c7c3b7759031408a6993e6def8ee036ed0124e8b802e1efa" :answer/id #uuid "d393fac0-eac0-5c1b-a3b0-a43744f37b23" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$st and $2$nd only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35757/selection/8c7626a29cdcabf55a88b5acac41dc4d33e615263d9fdae2a8d71b72a7ac7342" :answer/id #uuid "12d7424f-ba1b-5d15-8ee8-951e2d7a014b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$3$rd and $4$th only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35757/selection/0617f40c30d3177ee66fae7128600d63e0a36dcd56b2d8d825516d16b1bfc4ec" :answer/id #uuid "5f00ed0a-e660-5565-a95f-c21755c309d8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$3$rd only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35757/selection/39bbc673eae0cfa247f5c9