"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73620" :question/id #uuid "e65644f1-643f-5cec-a338-633970614cd1" :question/math-academy-id "q-73620" :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $A$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $A$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $2$nd and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot columns are the $3$rd and $5$th columns." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-73620/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5f0d2e9-1cf6-5fe4-85cc-f401382f39b2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73620"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73628/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "72a9936c-eec4-5e9c-9cdc-336f9478db9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73628/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "30bbef2e-2fd0-5828-b2a6-2e906ab10ac5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73628/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "e5d0c73d-931d-5007-9f09-b7ee492d651a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73628/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "86cb7ce6-8c81-5c20-82c1-a6530f21a4bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73628/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "ab144959-f7fb-526e-affe-55b12674c413" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73628/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a2a17f5c-678c-5ef4-84c5-4304085c2b85" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73628/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-73628/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-73628/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-73628/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-73628/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-73628/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73628" :question/id #uuid "cf960eda-9693-592c-b954-8f4bbda8185d" :question/math-academy-id "q-73628" :question/problem "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $B,$ given by\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 3 & -6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $B$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 3 & -6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & -8 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $B$ has $4$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-73628/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} 