6049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-130958" :question/id #uuid "2cb7299f-8b80-5020-a0a1-407df3d0dba1" :question/math-academy-id "q-130958" :question/problem "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $D,$ given by\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 0 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $D$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 0 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -4 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $D$ has $3$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-130958/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1073953e-7e0a-5237-8533-8882b7772741"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130958"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
